# 82. Real-Life Application Contexts

Prioritize contexts students can plausibly encounter.

Use:

- hourly wages with a flat fee or deduction;
- rental and service fees;
- ticket or fundraising goals;
- gym or subscription membership fees;
- simple budgeting scenarios;
- savings goals with a fixed contribution.

Avoid forcing artificial "real-world" contexts onto questions where a direct mathematical problem would be clearer.

