# 97. Quarter-Long Skills Reinforced This Week

Lesson 7 should continue reinforcing the larger Seminar III academic habits.

Students should practice:

## Reading Before Solving

Understand what an equation represents before choosing a solving strategy.

## Selecting a Strategy

Decide the correct order of inverse operations based on the equation's structure.

## Showing Enough Work to Diagnose Errors

Students should record each solving step, not just a final answer, so errors can be found.

## Checking

Substitute a solution back into the original equation before trusting it.

## Learning From Errors

Identify what happened and choose an appropriate response.

## Retrying

Use feedback to attempt the skill again.

